pySMESH: make StdMeshers_Prism_3D name the real reason it cannot mesh a prism whose side face
has a composite horizontal side, and forget the errors of the bottom candidates it rejected
(SMESH V9_16_0).

Defect: Prism_3D reports a solid as failed with the error of a FACE that it tried as the prism
bottom and rejected, and on a side face with a composite horizontal side it builds a mesh that
does not follow the EDGEs, which the stale error then hides.

Symptom: a straight prism on a regular n-gon, one bottom EDGE split at its midpoint, the top
EDGE above it whole, so the wall between them is one 5-EDGE FACE (report §3 B1). With
Regular_1D + NumberOfSegments(4), 2 on each half-EDGE, and Quadrangle_2D or MEFISTO_2D:
n = 5 fails with "Composite 'horizontal' edges are not supported", n = 6 with "Side face #27
has a composite top edge" (#27 is the top cap, not a side face), both "(algorithm Prism_3D)".
Prism_3D::Compute returns true for both.

Root cause, in StdMeshers_Prism_3D.cxx:
* initPrism() finds no FACE that must be the bottom: removeQuasiQuads() accepts the caps and
  the 5-EDGE wall as quadrangles. It then tries the FACEs one by one (:3740-3767), with
  mySetErrorToSM = false. The true bottom (n + 1 EDGEs) is skipped by "nbFaces < 2 + nbEdges"
  (:3758-3759); the 5-EDGE wall is rejected in getWallFaces() (:1162 for n = 5, :1251-1255 for
  n = 6); the top cap is accepted. Each rejection stores its message in the algorithm
  (SMESH_Algo::error) and nothing clears it. After Compute(), whatever it returned, the solid's
  sub-mesh takes the worse of its error and the algorithm's (SMESH_subMesh.cxx:1582), and
  checkComputeError() makes it FAILED_TO_COMPUTE (:2043-2060). The several-solid path clears
  the error after each candidate (InitComputeError(), :993-996); this path does not.
* With the top cap as bottom, the 5-EDGE wall has 1 EDGE on its bottom side and 2 on its top
  side. computeWalls() meshes the top side of a wall that is not meshed yet by projecting
  side[QUAD_BOTTOM_SIDE].grid->Edge(0) onto side[QUAD_TOP_SIDE].grid->Edge(0) only
  (:1925-1975): the first half-EDGE gets the 4 segments of the whole bottom EDGE, the second
  keeps its own 2. The caps then have 5 and 6 EDGEs, project2dMesh() cannot pair them, and
  projectBottomToTop() places the top nodes by the block approach (bottomToTopTrsf is always
  identity, GetLayersTransformation() being commented out). Measured with the stale error
  cleared: mesh volume off the prism volume by 1.7e-5 (n = 5, Quadrangle_2D) to 1.3e-3
  (n = 5, MEFISTO_2D) relative, 29 top cap nodes against 31 bottom ones, no vertical node
  column. A composite bottom side, which getWallFaces() accepts when all its EDGEs are on the
  bottom FACE, becomes a composite top side when initPrism() turns the prism upside down.
* The search is from SMESH 9a54694a0 (2013-02-12, "Merge from V6_main 11/02/2013"); upstream
  master at 83f8bf482 has the same code.

Change, in StdMeshers_Prism_3D.cxx only:
* getWallFaces(), first row of walls: a wall FACE that is not meshed yet and has more than one
  EDGE on its bottom or top side is refused, "Side face #N has B EDGE(s) on its bottom side and
  T on its top side; a composite horizontal side is not supported".
* initPrism(), search for a bottom: the reason of each FACE that is not the bottom is kept,
  "FACE #N: <its error>." or "FACE #N: not tried, it has E EDGEs and the solid F FACEs.". If a
  bottom is found, the stored error is cleared with error( COMPERR_OK ) (not
  InitComputeError(), which would also clear a cancel request). If none is found, the error is
  COMPERR_BAD_SHAPE "No FACE can be the bottom of the prism." followed by those reasons; before,
  its text was empty.

Not changed: the order of the candidates and the "2 + nbEdges" filter; a wall whose FACE is
already meshed; computeWalls() and the projections. A solid with no composite horizontal side
on an unmeshed wall meshes as before, bit for bit, unless a rejected candidate's error used to
fail it.

diff --git a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Prism_3D.cxx b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Prism_3D.cxx
--- a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Prism_3D.cxx
+++ b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Prism_3D.cxx
@@ -1160,6 +1160,19 @@
             for ( int iE = 0; iE < botSide->NbEdges(); ++iE )
               if ( !myHelper->IsSubShape( botSide->Edge(iE), thePrism.myBottom ))
                 return toSM( error(TCom("Composite 'horizontal' edges are not supported")));
+          }
+          // computeWalls() meshes the top side of a wall that is not meshed yet by projecting
+          // the first EDGE of its bottom side onto the first EDGE of its top side only, so a
+          // composite horizontal side gets a mesh that does not follow its EDGEs.
+          if ( !mesh->GetSubMesh( face )->IsMeshComputed() )
+          {
+            const int nbBotE = quadList.back()->side[ QUAD_BOTTOM_SIDE ].grid->NbEdges();
+            const int nbTopE = quadList.back()->side[ QUAD_TOP_SIDE    ].grid->NbEdges();
+            if ( nbBotE > 1 || nbTopE > 1 )
+              return toSM( error( COMPERR_BAD_SHAPE, TCom("Side face #") << shapeID( face )
+                                  << " has " << nbBotE << " EDGE(s) on its bottom side and "
+                                  << nbTopE << " on its top side; a composite horizontal side"
+                                  << " is not supported" ));
           }
           if ( faceMap.Add( face ))
           {
@@ -3741,6 +3754,7 @@
   {
     bool savedSetErrorToSM = mySetErrorToSM;
     mySetErrorToSM = false; // ignore errors in initPrism()
+    SMESH_Comment reasons; // why each FACE is not the bottom, reported if none is
 
     // search among meshed FACEs
     list< SMESH_subMesh* >::iterator sm = meshedSubMesh.begin();
@@ -3750,21 +3764,40 @@
       botSM             = *sm;
       thePrism.myBottom = TopoDS::Face( botSM->GetSubShape() );
       if ( !initPrism( thePrism, theShape3D, /*selectBottom=*/false ))
+      {
+        reasons << " FACE #" << shapeID( thePrism.myBottom ) << ": "
+                << ( _comment.empty() ? std::string( "rejected" ) : _comment ) << ".";
         botSM = NULL;
+      }
     }
     // search among all FACEs
     for ( TopExp_Explorer f( theShape3D, TopAbs_FACE ); !botSM && f.More(); f.Next() )
     {
       int minNbFaces = 2 + myHelper->Count( f.Current(), TopAbs_EDGE, false);
-      if ( nbFaces < minNbFaces) continue;
+      if ( nbFaces < minNbFaces)
+      {
+        reasons << " FACE #" << shapeID( f.Current() ) << ": not tried, it has "
+                << minNbFaces - 2 << " EDGEs and the solid " << nbFaces << " FACEs.";
+        continue;
+      }
       thePrism.Clear();
       thePrism.myBottom = TopoDS::Face( f.Current() );
       botSM             = myHelper->GetMesh()->GetSubMesh( thePrism.myBottom );
       if ( !initPrism( thePrism, theShape3D, /*selectBottom=*/false ))
+      {
+        reasons << " FACE #" << shapeID( thePrism.myBottom ) << ": "
+                << ( _comment.empty() ? std::string( "rejected" ) : _comment ) << ".";
         botSM = NULL;
+      }
     }
     mySetErrorToSM = savedSetErrorToSM;
-    return botSM ? true : toSM( error( COMPERR_BAD_SHAPE ));
+    if ( botSM )
+    {
+      error( COMPERR_OK ); // forget the errors of the rejected candidates
+      return true;
+    }
+    return toSM( error( COMPERR_BAD_SHAPE,
+                        SMESH_Comment( "No FACE can be the bottom of the prism." ) << reasons ));
   }
 
